You are implementing Upgrade-24 for zcoder: the Continuous Upgrade / Update / Feature Implementation Loop.

Goal
Build a bounded meta-orchestrator that repeatedly discovers and executes independently verifiable vertical slices across UPGRADE, UPDATE, IMPLEMENT_FEATURE, and REPAIR work while composing the existing Upgrade-20 autonomous engineering loop and Upgrade-23 maintenance intelligence.

Required invariants
1. Never run an unbounded autonomous loop. Enforce global iteration and no-progress budgets.
2. Execute one vertical slice per iteration and validate it before choosing the next item.
3. Deduplicate rediscovered work by stable content identity.
4. Keep provider/GitHub/shell side effects behind injected adapters or callbacks.
5. Treat newly introduced regressions as a hard stop by default.
6. Support rollback before retry/halt when the caller provides a rollback adapter.
7. Preserve structured checkpoints after every iteration and at final termination.
8. Keep Upgrade-20 responsible for task-level worktree, edit, validation, review, security, commit, push, PR, and CI-repair semantics.
9. Keep Upgrade-24 responsible for queue-level prioritization, work classification, retry/no-progress policy, and multi-item progression.
10. Maintain Python 3.9 compatibility and existing Clean Architecture dependency direction.

Implementation targets
- src/zcoder/services/upgrade_loop.py
- tests/unit/test_upgrade_loop.py
- docs/upgrades/UPGRADE-24.md
- exec-planning.md

Verification
Run the focused Upgrade-24 unit tests first, then the full repository suite. Do not weaken tests or gates to obtain green status. If a pre-existing failure exists, record baseline vs post-change delta and ensure the change introduces zero new regressions.

Completion criteria
- upgrade/update/feature/repair work kinds supported;
- priority ordering and discovery dedupe verified;
- bounded retries and no-progress detection verified;
- regression guard and rollback verified;
- checkpoints verified;
- Upgrade-23 recommendation adapter verified;
- full suite remains at least as green as the pre-change baseline.
